{"agent":"lane-show-corr","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new `history` parameter is declared `cli_only=True`, so it is not exposed to the MCP `show` action. An MCP client that requests the `show` action cannot set `history=true`; the action call therefore always evaluates `bool(a.get(\"history\"))` as false and the returned view can only show the latest correction per field, not the full correction list. This contradicts the stated acceptance/four-way configurability requirement [r-feature-four-ways], which calls for the same capability to be reachable from the MCP surface as well as CLI/JSON.","digest":"9f11416afc3227fe","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/reporting.py:309","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/reporting.py:309"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The secret-correction test only inspects `--history` and `--json`; it never runs the default `ddflow show T1` output. If `show` prints the corrected `body` field verbatim for a `--secret` correction while the `--json` and `--history` renderers redact it, this test still passes, so it does not enforce the acceptance rule that a secret correction must never show the secret from the verb a person uses.","digest":"0ca6b8239bdc30ae","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:test_a_secret_correction_shows_the_marker_and_no_values","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:test_a_secret_correction_shows_the_marker_and_no_values"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":14631,"diff_sha":"49ef7f93493da2b72f16b9dd22d6283d3fa89aaaa834ec86ee9f49fba3462694","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/REC-show-corrected-fields","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":278.1,"excluded_bytes":1577,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"05762cea0dfb6eb9","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/REC-show-corrected-fields.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T050918Z-3644e704.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"71aa3d8da45326ba8ddf704aafb2156064a4bc0b","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 e55a3d8cae0fdd80b14f90602beead9d8a0c1cc6","ddflow/api/reporting/records.py":"100644 304f0781ce312ffb47ed9d0d37c970a164a3099f","ddflow/surfaces/commands/reporting.py":"100644 dfbdb8846d674512e6c8d13836b3cf19cf10983e","ddflow/surfaces/declared/reporting.py":"100644 804301be0cc3476a6d88e5916f1656169998269e","ddflow/views/markdown/report.py":"100644 797413d5c232819d7fbda317e0d08b8da259322f","tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py":"100644 af874de65d56c6b58427db5e54b6db6ed6118216"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/declared/reporting.py:309","tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:test_a_secret_correction_shows_the_marker_and_no_values"],"tree_sha":"71aa3d8da453+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e749111cd4eaf44920b63c77a","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":190219,"schema":1,"subject":"REC-show-corrected-fields","ts":"2026-11-13T05:14:00.750916Z"}
{"agent":"lane-show-corr","data":{"gate":"critic"},"id":"e6fe7889967982c44558ea206","kind":"gate.started","lamport":190224,"schema":1,"subject":"REC-show-corrected-fields","ts":"2026-11-13T05:14:13.572659Z"}
{"agent":"lane-show-corr","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new `history` flag is declared `cli_only=True`, so the MCP/JSON surface generated from this declared action cannot request correction history. A client that calls the MCP `show` action with `history=true` (or expects the same `ddflow show --history` capability through the declared API) gets `a.get(\"history\")` absent/false, so the call lambda passes `history=False` to `A.show`; the view then only prints the latest correction per field and never the full correction list. That makes the history capability CLI-only, violating the four-way/record-parity acceptance that the same show capability is available in MCP and JSON, not only in the CLI. [r-feature-four-ways]","digest":"c6aab322128a6944","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/reporting.py:304","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/reporting.py:304"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The `--secret` test only checks `--history` and `--json`; it never runs the default `show` output. For input `correct T1 --field body --text SECRET --reason ... --secret`, an implementation can redact the correction history and JSON while still printing the current `body` value in the normal markdown report, so `SECRET` is visible on the primary `show` surface, yet the test passes because it only asserts `SECRET not in --json + --history`. The test also loops over `data[\"corrections\"][0][\"fields\"]` without asserting that list is non-empty, so an empty JSON `fields` array would also pass despite the acceptance requirement that corrected fields be exposed.","digest":"a50a97c35e77e736","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:85","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:85"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test named “appear only when the knobs are on” only tests the knob-on case: it enables `correct_digest_new` and asserts `row[\"new\"]` is truthy. No test runs a non-secret correction with the default knobs and asserts that `row[\"old\"]` and `row[\"new\"]` are empty. Given an implementation that ignores `correct_digest_new` and always emits a digest, the suite still passes: `test_show_prints_author_model_and_the_corrected_marker` only checks that the raw old value is absent, and `test_json_adds_fields_and_keeps_the_existing_ones` never inspects `fields`, so the “only when the knobs are on” requirement is not actually verified.","digest":"133f02252ca2b5fb","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:91","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:91"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The MCP test only asserts `author_model` and `corrections[0][\"reason\"]`. An MCP `show` result that omits `by`, `at`, or `fields` (or returns an empty `fields` list) still passes, while the acceptance criterion says the same correction fields must appear in the MCP action. Given a response containing `{\"author_model\": \"model-right\", \"corrections\": [{\"reason\": \"fix\"}]}`, the test passes even though the MCP surface is missing the marker fields required by `r-record-parity`-style parity.","digest":"78487f6f016698de","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:150","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:150"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":14631,"diff_sha":"49ef7f93493da2b72f16b9dd22d6283d3fa89aaaa834ec86ee9f49fba3462694","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/REC-show-corrected-fields","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":389.4,"excluded_bytes":1577,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"alibaba","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"348329384a17fab5","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/REC-show-corrected-fields.critic.[REDACTED:name].20261113T051413Z-5ec8ae65.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794547243.2011867,"family":"google","gate":"critic","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"},{"at":1794547243.3129342,"family":"xai","gate":"critic","model":"grok-4.7","reason":"HTTP 403","reviewer":"grok-4.7"}],"review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"71aa3d8da45326ba8ddf704aafb2156064a4bc0b","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 e55a3d8cae0fdd80b14f90602beead9d8a0c1cc6","ddflow/api/reporting/records.py":"100644 304f0781ce312ffb47ed9d0d37c970a164a3099f","ddflow/surfaces/commands/reporting.py":"100644 dfbdb8846d674512e6c8d13836b3cf19cf10983e","ddflow/surfaces/declared/reporting.py":"100644 804301be0cc3476a6d88e5916f1656169998269e","ddflow/views/markdown/report.py":"100644 797413d5c232819d7fbda317e0d08b8da259322f","tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py":"100644 af874de65d56c6b58427db5e54b6db6ed6118216"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/declared/reporting.py:304","tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:85","tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:91","tests/test_show_corrected_fields.py:150"],"tree_sha":"71aa3d8da453+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"4 finding(s)"},"id":"ee60d5838b536ffc44b7907d7","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":190305,"schema":1,"subject":"REC-show-corrected-fields","ts":"2026-11-13T05:20:43.789637Z"}
